AU  - Jacob, Daniel Etim; Nеlson, Imaobong Ufot; Izah, Sylvester Chibueze; Ukpong, Eteakamba; Akpan, Unyime Ukpong; Ogwu, Matthew Chidozie
TI  - Bioindicators in Recreational Planning and Development: Balancing Nature and Human Activities
PY  - 2024
AB  - Bioindicators play a crucial role in the sustainable progress of recreational planning and development, functioning as essential tools that offer a deep understanding of the complex relationship between human activities and the health of ecosystems. This chapter highlights the crucial role of bioindicators in developing sustainable recreational planning approaches, where the balance between nature conservation and human leisure activities is carefully maintained. This chapter extensively examines the various bioindicators that are crucial for assessing environmental changes and highlights their important roles in decision-making processes. Furthermore, it reveals possible obstacles linked to their successful execution within the framework of recreational planning. It also presents strategic frameworks by understanding the intricate dynamics that support the synergy between bioindicators and recreational planning cum development. These frameworks serve the dual purpose of protecting our natural reserves and creating well-designed pathways for recreational activities, thus promoting a mutually beneficial interaction between humans and the environment.
