TI  - Sonic Patterns I: The Noise
PY  - 2013
AB  - Noise can be defined as a sound with a poor information or simply an unwanted sound that can mask other sounds. Accordingly, the source of noise may be of natural (geophonies, biophonies) or manmade (anthrophonies) origin. The noise produced by human activities has grown quite rapidly in the past century, over the larger part of the Earth. Noise reduces the distance from the sender at which a signal can be detected by a receiver. This distance is called active space and represents an important parameter in communication.
